.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Les Allen and coworkers showed that Laguerre-Gaussian light modes carrying a helical (spiral) phase front e^{il\phi} possess a well-defined orbital angular momentum of l\hbar per photon -- an intrinsic, mechanical property of light entirely separate from the spin angular momentum carried by polarization. The discovery opened the field of structured light and optical vortices. laguerre_gaussian_mode constructs the \mathrm{LG}_p^l mode amplitude">

